 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'Enable "Add noise to canvas readback", visit a canvas-fingerprint test page (or run a canvas `toDataURL()` script twice across two fresh tabs/sessions) - **Expected:** the resulting data URL/hash differs between sessions even on an identical canvas draw.', 198),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'Enable "Normalize screen dimensions", open DevTools console, run `screen.width` / `screen.height` - **Expected:** values are rounded to the nearest 50px rather than the monitor''s exact resolution.', 199),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'Enable "Letterbox the page viewport", resize the browser window across several sizes, checking `window.innerWidth`/`innerHeight` in DevTools console - **Expected:** values snap to multiples of the bucket size (default 200x100px) with visible solid-color bars filling the remainder of the tab area.', 200),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'With both screen-normalize and letterboxing enabled, compare `screen.width` to `window.innerWidth` in console - **Expected:** the two values match (so a site can''t cross-check one faked value against the other).', 201),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'Open DevTools **docked** to the side with letterboxing on - **Expected:** the page viewport is still a clean bucket multiple, not `total_width - devtools_width`.', 202),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Fingerprint Resistance Suite (Canvas Noise, Screen Metrics, Letterboxing)', N'Disable all three toggles - **Expected:** canvas output is stable/deterministic again, `screen.width`/`height` report real values, and no letterbox bars appear.', 203),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'Browse a few sites that load third-party resources (news sites, sites with embedded ad/analytics scripts), then open `chrome://tracking-dashboard` - **Expected:** stat cards show non-zero "trackers" and "sites" counts, and a graph renders with blue (first-party) and orange (third-party) nodes connected by edges.', 204),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'Hover/inspect the graph - **Expected:** the layout animates to a stable position (spring-physics simulation), not a static snapshot.', 205),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'Click "Clear data" - **Expected:** stat cards reset to zero and the graph empties.', 206),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'Restart the browser and revisit the dashboard (without clearing first) - **Expected:** previously recorded relationships persist (loaded from the per-profile LevelDB store), confirming it survives restarts.', 207),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'As of v1.8.27: visit a site with no recorded trackers yet - **Expected:** the toolbar button shows no badge. Then visit a site known to trigger third-party requests - **Expected:** a numeric badge appears on the button showing the tracker count for that site (a "9+" placeholder above 9), and clicking the button opens `chrome://tracking-dashboard` as a normal tab, not a bubble.', 208),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'As of v1.8.27: with the badge showing a count on one tab, switch to a different tab with a different (or zero) tracker count - **Expected:** the badge updates or hides to match the newly active tab''s site, without needing a page reload.', 209),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Tracking Relationship Dashboard', N'As of v1.8.27: with the dashboard button visible, flip pref `toolbar.show_tracking_dashboard_button` to `false` (e.g. via a temporary pref edit) - **Expected:** the button disappears immediately, matching `PrivacyShieldButton`''s own visibility-pref pattern.', 210),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Incognito Clipboard Privacy', N'Open an incognito window, copy some text from a page, then close that incognito window (as the last/only incognito window open) - **Expected:** pasting anywhere (e.g. into the omnibox or a text editor) afterward yields nothing / an empty clipboard.', 211),
