 (N'Privacy & Security', N'De-Googling & Privacy-Safe Defaults', N'Browse a few ordinary sites with DevTools Network tab open (filter by domain) - **Expected:** no outbound requests to `google-analytics.com`, `doubleclick.net`, or other Google telemetry endpoints originating from the browser itself (as opposed to sites you visit making their own such requests).', 247),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'De-Googling & Privacy-Safe Defaults', N'Visit `chrome://settings/help` (About page) - **Expected:** a "Chromium" version row appears alongside the browser''s own version string.', 248),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'De-Googling & Privacy-Safe Defaults', N'(If telemetry hardening was applied at build time) Confirm via `chrome://net-internals` or packet capture that pruned endpoints (e.g. `clients2.google.com`, `safebrowsing.googleapis.com`) are never contacted - **Expected:** no connection attempts logged to these hosts.', 249),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Google API Key InfoBar Suppression', N'Launch the browser fresh (new profile, no API keys configured) - **Expected:** no yellow "Google API keys missing" InfoBar appears on the initial window or new tab.', 250),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Google API Key InfoBar Suppression', N'Open several new tabs and windows - **Expected:** the InfoBar never appears in any of them.', 251),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Google API Key InfoBar Suppression', N'Confirm no functional regression - sign-in, Safe Browsing, and other features that would normally use API keys still behave normally (no crashes/errors attributable to the suppression) - **Expected:** browser behaves normally aside from the banner''s absence.', 252),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'WebRTC IP Leak Protection', N'With the toggle in its default (enabled) state, visit a WebRTC IP leak test page (e.g. any public "WebRTC leak test" site) - **Expected:** only the public IP is listed; no `192.168.x.x` / `10.x.x.x` local address appears.', 253),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'WebRTC IP Leak Protection', N'Disable the toggle and revisit the same test page - **Expected:** local LAN IP address(es) may now appear in the WebRTC candidate list.', 254),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'WebRTC IP Leak Protection', N'Re-enable the toggle - **Expected:** local IP disappears again; video/voice call functionality (test with any WebRTC call demo) still works normally.', 255),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Additional Hardening Defaults (Guest Mode, Battery API, About Page)', N'Check the profile/people menu (click the avatar / profile icon) - **Expected:** no "Open Guest window" / "Guest" entry appears by default.', 256),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Additional Hardening Defaults (Guest Mode, Battery API, About Page)', N'Open `chrome://settings` and locate the guest-mode setting - **Expected:** it is present and off by default; toggling it on and restarting **Expected:** the Guest option reappears in the profile menu.', 257),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Additional Hardening Defaults (Guest Mode, Battery API, About Page)', N'Visit any HTTPS page, open DevTools console, run `navigator.getBattery === undefined ? ''unsupported'' : navigator.getBattery().then(b => console.log(b.level, b.charging))` - **Expected:** the call either resolves with no meaningful/real data or the connection is silently closed with no crash - critically, **the page/renderer does not crash** even though the API is called.', 258),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Additional Hardening Defaults (Guest Mode, Battery API, About Page)', N'Open `chrome://settings/help` - **Expected:** a "Chromium" row with a version string appears in addition to the browser''s own version.', 259),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'Open Settings -> Privacy and security -> Timezone override - **Expected:** select shows "System default" selected on a fresh profile.', 260),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'In any regular page''s console, note the current values of `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone` and `new Date().getTimezoneOffset()`.', 261),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'Back on the Settings page, select a zone far from your real one (e.g. "Asia/Tokyo") - **Expected:** applies immediately, no restart.', 262),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'Re-check `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone` and `new Date().getTimezoneOffset()` in an existing or new tab - **Expected:** both now reflect Tokyo time (`"Asia/Tokyo"`, and an offset of `-540` minutes), differing from the machine''s real timezone.', 263),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'Restart the browser (without reverting the override) - **Expected:** the override persists across restart (re-applied from the saved pref on profile load) - the Settings page still shows the overridden zone selected, and `Intl.DateTimeFormat()` still reports it.', 264),
 (N'Privacy & Security', N'Timezone Override (Anti-Fingerprinting)', N'Revert to "System default" - **Expected:** the browser''s reported timezone reverts to the real host system timezone (verify via `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone`).', 265),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Open `chrome://settings/customProxy` - **Expected:** Page loads with mode radio buttons (System / Direct / Auto-detect / PAC URL / Manual).', 266),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Select "Auto-detect" and Apply - **Expected:** Config applies immediately, no restart required.', 267),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Select "Manual proxy", enter a single proxy `host:port`, Apply - **Expected:** Subsequent traffic routes through that proxy.', 268),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Switch to per-scheme mode and set different HTTP/HTTPS proxies - **Expected:** Each protocol uses its own assigned proxy.', 269),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Add a bypass rule (e.g. `localhost`) - **Expected:** Bypassed hosts load directly, not via the proxy.', 270),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Click "Clear" - **Expected:** Resets to OS system default proxy.', 271),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Open `chrome://proxy/` - **Expected:** Same config is visible/editable (all three surfaces share state via the same `apply`/`clear` messages).', 272),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Proxy Settings', N'Edge case: enter a malformed PAC URL and Apply - **Expected:** No crash; config reports pending/failed state rather than silently succeeding.', 273),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Look at the toolbar on a fresh profile - **Expected:** Globe icon present, inactive state (no rules yet).', 274),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Navigate to `chrome://custom-settings/proxy-routing` and add a rule (pattern `*.httpbin.org`, proxy `PROXY 127.0.0.1:8888`) - **Expected:** Rule appears in the table.', 275),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'With a local proxy running on port 8888, navigate to `https://httpbin.org/ip` - **Expected:** Reported IP is the proxy''s outbound IP, not the local machine''s.', 276),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Open `chrome://net-internals/#proxy` - **Expected:** An active PAC script is shown containing a `shExpMatch` clause for `*.httpbin.org`.', 277),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Click the toolbar globe icon - **Expected:** Status bubble opens showing "Active - 1 rule".', 278),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Toggle routing off from the bubble - **Expected:** Icon reverts to inactive; net-internals shows `mode: SYSTEM`.', 279),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Disable the rule via its per-rule toggle in settings (without disabling routing globally) - **Expected:** PAC regenerates without that clause; traffic to the domain goes direct again.', 280),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Smart Proxy Routing', N'Edge case: configure a manual proxy in Proxy Settings first, then enable Smart Proxy Routing - **Expected:** A warning is shown, since routing will overwrite the manual proxy config with the generated PAC.', 281),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Click a `magnet:` link on any webpage - **Expected:** Tab redirects to `chrome://bittorrent`; torrent appears and moves from Queued -> Downloading as metadata resolves.', 282),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Download a `.torrent` file and let it complete downloading (as a file, not a torrent) - **Expected:** It''s automatically detected, added to the torrent manager, the temp file is deleted, and the tab redirects to `chrome://bittorrent`.', 283),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'In Windows Explorer, double-click a `.torrent` file (after setting the browser as default handler in settings) - **Expected:** Browser launches/foregrounds and opens the torrent in the manager.', 284),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'In `chrome://bittorrent`, click Pause then Resume on an active torrent - **Expected:** State changes to Paused (network activity stops) then back to Downloading.', 285),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Click "Open Folder" on a torrent - **Expected:** Opens the save path in the OS file manager.', 286),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Remove a torrent with "delete files" checked - **Expected:** Torrent disappears from the list and downloaded data is deleted from disk.', 287),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Go to `chrome://settings/bittorrent` -> File association section, click "Set as default" then "Remove" - **Expected:** OS `.torrent` association is registered, then cleared (verify via Windows "Default apps" or re-double-clicking a `.torrent` file).', 288),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Adjust max download/upload KiB/s and max connections, restart the browser - **Expected:** Settings persist and visibly cap transfer rates.', 289),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Integrated BitTorrent Client', N'Edge case: turn off the master enable toggle in settings - **Expected:** Toolbar/bottom-bar buttons disappear (or stop working) and magnet links are no longer intercepted.', 290),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Start a large download from a server that supports HTTP Range requests - **Expected:** Download begins normally and is visible in `chrome://downloads`.', 291),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Mid-download, force-kill the browser process (Task Manager, not a normal quit) - **Expected:** Download is left in an interrupted state.', 292),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Relaunch the browser - **Expected:** Without clicking anything, the download automatically resumes from where it stopped (progress continues, not restarting from 0%).', 293),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Let it finish - **Expected:** File completes successfully and is valid/openable.', 294),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Edge case: repeat the crash test against a server that does NOT support Range requests, or delete the partial file before relaunch - **Expected:** Download cannot auto-resume and is left interrupted, requiring a manual retry.', 295),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Crash-Resilient Downloads', N'Edge case: set `custom.download.auto_resume_interrupted` to `false` via the pref bridge, repeat the crash test - **Expected:** Interrupted download stays interrupted after relaunch; manual "Resume" click is required.', 296),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Start a file download - **Expected:** Download shelf appears at the bottom of the window with a visibly enhanced progress indicator.', 297),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Let all active downloads finish - **Expected:** If auto-hide is enabled, the shelf hides itself automatically once nothing is in progress.', 298),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Trigger a download''s options/details control - **Expected:** A download options view surfaces (location, naming/collision handling, security settings), if the options dialog is enabled.', 299),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Complete a download - **Expected:** A completion notification appears with "Open" and "Show in Folder" action buttons.', 300),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Change the configured custom download path, then download another file - **Expected:** The new file saves to the custom directory rather than the previous default.', 301),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Advanced Download Management', N'Edge case: download a file type Chromium flags as dangerous - **Expected:** Advanced dangerous-download handling/controls appear rather than the stock warning only.', 302),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Navigate to an Instagram post or reel URL - **Expected:** A floating Save button appears bottom-right.', 303),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Click Save on a single photo post - **Expected:** Image downloads straight to the Downloads folder with no "Save As" prompt.', 304),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Click Save on a reel/video - **Expected:** Video file downloads directly, same no-prompt behavior.', 305),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Click Save on a carousel (multi-image) post - **Expected:** Every slide downloads as a separate file (Chromium''s own multi-download infobar may appear once several downloads fire in a tab).', 306),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'After opening a post/reel directly, browse to a grid/feed/profile page containing that same post - **Expected:** A small heart badge appears on its thumbnail if you''d previously liked it.', 307),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'While viewing a single post, like or unlike it using Instagram''s own like button - **Expected:** The badge/liked state updates to match without needing to reload.', 308),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Go to Instagram Settings -> Your Activity -> Interactions -> Likes ("Liked posts"), then find the injected "Sync all my likes" button - **Expected:** Clicking it auto-scrolls the full liked-posts list and bulk-populates heart badges for everything in it, without opening each post individually.', 309),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Edge case: uncheck the like-status badge toggle in Settings mid-session - **Expected:** Badges stop appearing and no further grid-mutation work happens (not just hidden - the observer actually stops).', 310),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Instagram Downloader', N'Edge case: view an Instagram Story - **Expected:** No Save button appears; Stories use a different URL/API not covered by this feature.', 311),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Launch the browser, then close it cleanly via the window''s close button - **Expected:** After a moment, `startup_cache.json` in the profile folder shows `"last_clean_shutdown": true`.', 312),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Launch again and inspect the file within the first ~5 seconds - **Expected:** File still reflects the prior session''s data; no write has landed yet (deferred flush).', 313),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Wait 5+ seconds after that same launch, then re-check the file - **Expected:** `launch_count` incremented by 1 and `last_startup_time` updated to the current session''s timestamp.', 314),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Force-kill the browser process (Task Manager) after waiting past the 5-second mark - **Expected:** File on disk shows `"last_clean_shutdown": false` (written by the earlier deferred flush, never updated to `true` since shutdown was never clean).', 315),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Relaunch the browser - **Expected:** The crash is detected internally (`PreviousSessionCrashed()` returns true); cross-check by confirming any interrupted downloads from that session auto-resume (see Crash-Resilient Downloads above), which relies on this same signal.', 316),
 (N'Network & Downloads', N'Startup Cache', N'Edge case: manually edit `startup_cache.json` to exceed 4 KB (pad it with data) and relaunch - **Expected:** Browser treats the oversized file as corrupt, discards it, and starts with a fresh cache rather than crashing.', 317),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Navigate to a page known to publish an RSS feed (e.g. a typical blog or news site) - **Expected:** An infobar appears reading "RSS feed detected: \<title\>" with two buttons, **Subscribe** and **Cancel**.', 318),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Click **Subscribe** - **Expected:** Infobar dismisses; the feed is added to your subscriptions (no visible confirmation dialog, but it now appears in the reader sidebar).', 319),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Open `chrome://reader` - **Expected:** Reader UI loads with the newly subscribed feed listed in the sidebar (Ungrouped section) without needing to reload the reader tab.', 320),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Click into the feed and open an article - **Expected:** Article content renders in the reading pane; the item is marked read and the feed''s unread count decrements.', 321),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Create a new folder/group in the sidebar and drag or move the feed into it - **Expected:** Feed moves out of "Ungrouped" into the new group; sidebar reflects the new organization.', 322),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Use the reader''s OPML export, then import it back (or into a fresh profile) - **Expected:** All subscriptions and groupings are restored intact.', 323),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Return to a page with a feed you already subscribed to and check the infobar behavior; then visit a new RSS page and click **Cancel** instead of Subscribe - **Expected:** Already-subscribed feeds don''t re-prompt (`IsKnownChannelURL` skips them); Cancel simply dismisses with no subscription created.', 324),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Toggle dark mode (OS or browser theme) while the reader tab is open - **Expected:** Reader UI switches to its dark theme.', 325),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Click **(refresh) Refresh** in the reader header - **Expected:** button shows a brief spin; feeds refresh regardless of their normal update interval.', 326),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Click **All feeds** - **Expected:** aggregated item list across every feed, with a summed unread badge.', 327),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Type in **Search articles** - **Expected:** debounced (~250ms) results filter to matching titles; clearing the box restores the previous feed/group view.', 328),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Switch item-list layout using the **Title / Magazine / Full** buttons - **Expected:** Title/Magazine/Full views render distinctly (thumbnail in Magazine, full image + "Open original article" button in Full); selection persists across a reload.', 329),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'Toggle RSS off from Settings while `chrome://reader` is open in another tab - **Expected:** the reader tab live-swaps to the disabled-message screen without a manual reload.', 330),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'As of v1.8.28: open `chrome://reader` on a fresh profile with zero subscriptions - **Expected:** a categorized starter-feed picker (Tech/News/Science/Culture) appears in the main pane instead of "Select a feed to read articles." Check a few feeds and click "Add N feeds" - **Expected:** the picker disappears and the reader switches to the normal feed view with the selected feeds subscribed.', 331),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'As of v1.8.28: subscribe to a feed, then repoint its URL at something that will fail (a 404 or a dead host) and let it attempt at least 3 fetches (use (refresh) Refresh to force attempts rather than waiting out the update interval) - **Expected:** a small (warning) appears next to the feed''s title in the sidebar, with a tooltip explaining it hasn''t updated successfully in a while.', 332),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'As of v1.8.28: repoint that same feed back to a working URL and let one fetch succeed ((refresh) Refresh) - **Expected:** the (warning) indicator clears.', 333),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'RSS Reader', N'As of v1.8.28: with existing subscriptions from a pre-upgrade profile (schema v3), launch the upgraded browser - **Expected:** all existing subscriptions are intact (the v3->v4 migration adds columns in place; it must not wipe the database).', 334),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Click a link on a web page pointing to an `http://` or `https://` URL ending in `.epub` - **Expected:** Navigation is intercepted and redirected to `chrome://epub-reader/?url=<encoded-url>`, book opens and renders.', 335),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Navigate directly to `chrome://epub-reader/?url=file:///path/to/book.epub` - **Expected:** Local EPUB loads and renders via epub.js.', 336),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Click the toolbar **"Open file..."** button and pick a local `.epub` from disk - **Expected:** Book loads directly from the file picker without needing a URL at all.', 337),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Use the prev/next controls and the Table of Contents panel - **Expected:** Page turns / jumping to a TOC entry navigates within the book.', 338),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Increase/decrease font size and change theme (light / dark / sepia / auto) - **Expected:** Text resizes and colors update live inside the book viewer, without re-rendering the whole book; "auto" follows the OS light/dark setting.', 339),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Toggle paginated vs. scrolled mode - **Expected:** Reading flow switches between page-turn and continuous scroll.', 340),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Read partway into a book, close the tab, and reopen the same book URL - **Expected:** Reading position (last CFI/progress) is restored automatically.', 341),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'ePub Reader', N'Try navigating directly to a `file:///path/to/book.epub` URL (not via `chrome://epub-reader/`) - **Expected:** Known limitation - the auto-redirect throttle only intercepts http/https, so this does *not* redirect; you must use the explicit `chrome://epub-reader/?url=file://...` form.', 342),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'Navigate to a clearly article-style page (news article, blog post) - **Expected:** Since auto-detect is off by default, no automatic prompt appears; manually invoke the reader-mode command/context-menu item to check availability.', 343),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'Right-click on the article page and select **"Enter Reader Mode"** (or trigger command 35083) - **Expected:** Brief "Distilling" state, then content is replaced with the clean reader layout (centered column, serif font, white content card).', 344),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'Right-click again while in reader mode - **Expected:** Menu now offers **"Exit Reader Mode"**; selecting it returns the page to normal rendering.', 345),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'Try triggering reader mode on a non-article page (e.g. a search results page, a `chrome://` page, or a page with mostly navigation/no article body) - **Expected:** Command is unavailable/greyed out, or reports "Not Available" - no distillation attempted on excluded schemes (`chrome://`, `about:`, `data:`, etc).', 346),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'Trigger reader mode on a page likely to fail distillation (e.g. a very sparse or malformed page) - **Expected:** State moves to "Error" and the UI fails gracefully rather than showing broken/garbled content.', 347),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Reader Mode Integration', N'(Edge, requires a build with auto-detect flipped on) Navigate to several article pages in a row - **Expected:** Reader-mode availability is automatically flagged per page without manual triggering.', 348),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Open any regular web page, then click the **Top Sites** toolbar icon - **Expected:** A ~380x300px bubble opens (no title bar/close button) showing a 4-column grid of top-site tiles with favicons and titles.', 349),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Left-click a tile - **Expected:** Current tab navigates to that site; bubble closes.', 350),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Middle-click a tile (or right-click -> "Open in new tab") - **Expected:** Site opens in a new background tab; bubble stays open.', 351),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Right-click a tile -> **Remove** - **Expected:** Tile disappears immediately and the grid reflows.', 352),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Click the Top Sites toolbar icon again while the bubble is open - **Expected:** Bubble closes (toggle behavior).', 353),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Open a new tab (NTP) after removing/interacting with tiles from the panel - **Expected:** NTP shows the same updated tile set, confirming shared state with the panel.', 354),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Most Visited Panel', N'Open the panel in an Incognito window - **Expected:** Empty-state message (or empty grid) since `RemoteNtpService` is unavailable for that profile.', 355),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Open the sidebar and click the **Notes** button - **Expected:** Notes panel loads, header shows the normalized domain/URL of the current tab.', 356),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'With an empty note for the current page, type some text and let it sit ~1 second, then close the sidebar without clicking Save, then reopen Notes - **Expected:** Your draft text is still there (auto-saved to a local draft after 300ms, restored on reopen).', 357),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Click **Save** - **Expected:** Note is persisted; draft is cleared.', 358),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Navigate to a `chrome://` or `file://` page (not http/https) - **Expected:** Notes editor shows no active URL / notes are unavailable for that page.', 359),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Switch to a different http/https tab - **Expected:** Notes header and content update live to the new tab''s URL without a manual refresh.', 360),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Add a second note to the same page - **Expected:** A multi-note list appears below the editor; clicking a row loads that note into the editor for editing.', 361),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Expand the **All notes** section and use the search box - **Expected:** List filters client-side by URL or note text across all saved notes.', 362),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'Open the same page in an Incognito window and check Notes - **Expected:** Notes from the regular profile are visible and editable (incognito redirects to the parent profile''s notes).', 363),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'Page Notes', N'(If wanderlust-api backend/cloud-sync sign-in is configured) Click **Share note publicly** - **Expected:** Note appears in the "Shared annotations" list with your display name; if not signed in via cloud sync, a "backend not configured" notice is shown instead.', 364),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'Open the sidebar and click the **AI Page Assistant** button - **Expected:** Chat panel opens at `chrome://sidebar/agent` showing an empty message list and an input box. If no backend/API key is configured, at minimum confirm the panel opens cleanly and shows a sensible empty/error state rather than a blank or broken page.', 365),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'With no API key configured, type a question and press Enter - **Expected:** A "Thinking..." indicator appears briefly, then an error message is shown (e.g. missing/invalid key) rather than a hang or crash.', 366),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'If a working API key is configured (Settings -> AI page -> password field), navigate to a content-heavy page and ask a question about it - **Expected:** "Thinking..." indicator, then a reply from Claude that reflects the visible page text.', 367),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'Ask the assistant to perform an action on the page (e.g. "click the login button for you") - **Expected:** Assistant declines and explains it can only read/discuss the page, not act on it.', 368),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'Close the sidebar (or navigate away) and reopen the Agent panel - **Expected:** Prior conversation turns are restored (transcript persists in-memory for the browser session).', 369),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'Click **Clear** (clear history) - **Expected:** Transcript empties immediately.', 370),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'AI Page Assistant', N'Navigate to a different page and ask a new question without clearing - **Expected:** Old conversation turns remain visible (transcript is not per-tab/per-URL scoped), but the new answer is based on the newly-visited page''s content.', 371),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Right-click on a JavaScript-dependent page - **Expected:** Context menu shows a JavaScript control option to **block** JS (since current state is "allow/default").', 372),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Click **"Block JavaScript on this page"** - **Expected:** JavaScript is blocked; JS-dependent content/behavior on the page stops working.', 373),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Reload the page - **Expected:** JavaScript remains blocked (setting persisted via `HostContentSettingsMap`, not just an in-session toggle).', 374),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Right-click again and select **"Allow JavaScript on this page"** - **Expected:** JavaScript is re-enabled; if the doc''s "real-time application" claim holds, functionality resumes without a reload - otherwise verify it takes effect on next reload.', 375),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Right-click and select **"Use default setting"** - **Expected:** Per-site override is cleared; page reverts to the browser''s global JavaScript default.', 376),
 (N'Content & Reading', N'JavaScript Content Controls', N'Set a Block override on one domain, then visit a different, unrelated domain - **Expected:** The second domain is unaffected (setting is scoped per URL/domain, not global).', 377),
